So it's been a while.
所以已经过去很久了。

170
00:06:05.270 --> 00:06:08.310
And he is also back as our showrunner.
而且他也回归担任我们的剧集运作人。

171
00:06:08.990 --> 00:06:09.350
Yes.
是的。

172
00:06:09.510 --> 00:06:10.470
For the whole season.
整个这一季都是。

173
00:06:10.750 --> 00:06:11.830
We were so excited.
我们当时太兴奋了。

174
00:06:12.170 --> 00:06:17.550
Greg gave an interview to Variety where he talked a little bit about his vision for this season.
格雷格接受了《综艺》杂志的采访，谈到了他对这一季的一些构想。

175
00:06:18.210 --> 00:06:23.530
First of all, he said, we will not be telling the story of who is in the manager's chair.
首先，他说，我们不会再讲谁来坐经理宝座的故事了。

176
00:06:23.930 --> 00:06:26.990
Who is manager is no longer a story.
谁当经理不再是一个故事线了。

177
00:06:27.310 --> 00:06:28.130
Thank the Lord.
谢天谢地。

178
00:06:28.350 --> 00:06:28.730
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

179
00:06:28.990 --> 00:06:29.590
You know what?
你知道吗？

180
00:06:29.590 --> 00:06:30.890
I was done with that.
我受够那个了。

181
00:06:31.030 --> 00:06:31.510
Me too.
我也是。

182
00:06:31.750 --> 00:06:32.890
Not that anyone asked.
虽然没人问我。

183
00:06:34.650 --> 00:06:36.550
I think we were all done with it.
我想我们都受够了。

184
00:06:36.670 --> 00:06:36.810
Yeah.
是啊。

185
00:06:37.390 --> 00:06:42.290
Greg said instead he hoped to focus on big arcs in relationships.
格雷格说，他希望转而关注人物关系中的重大转折。

186
00:06:42.970 --> 00:06:43.650
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

187
00:06:43.650 --> 00:06:48.130
He also wanted to write stories where different characters were the lead of each episode.
他还想写一些让不同角色成为每一集主角的故事。

188
00:06:48.130 --> 00:06:50.350
And you're going to really see that in season nine.
你会在第九季中真正看到这一点。

189
00:06:50.810 --> 00:06:53.950
Each of our characters is going to have a real nice A story.
我们的每个角色都会有一条非常精彩的主线故事。

190
00:06:54.690 --> 00:07:01.690
Greg also announced that all of the questions about who was behind the documentary would be answered this year.
格雷格还宣布，关于谁在拍摄这部纪录片的所有疑问，今年都会得到解答。

191
00:07:02.290 --> 00:07:03.130
Dun-dun-dun.
当当当。

192
00:07:03.130 --> 00:07:03.330
Hmm.
嗯。

193
00:07:04.270 --> 00:07:12.130
So something I think everyone should know is that when we started shooting this episode, we did not know that season nine would be the last season of The Office.
所以我想大家应该知道一件事，当我们开始拍摄这一集时，我们并不知道第九季会是《办公室》的最后一季。

194
00:07:12.870 --> 00:07:15.590
They did not tell us that until we were shooting Work Bus.
直到拍摄《工作巴士》那集时，他们才告诉我们。

195
00:07:15.990 --> 00:07:19.270
We talked about this in our book, The Office BFFs.
我们在我们的书《办公室闺蜜》里谈到过这一点。

196
00:07:19.710 --> 00:07:21.310
That would be the first book I've written.
那是我写的第一本书。

197
00:07:23.110 --> 00:07:24.690
Yeah, we didn't know yet.
是啊，我们当时还不知道。

198
00:07:24.690 --> 00:07:29.390
Yeah, but by the time this episode aired, we did know.
是啊，但等到这一集播出的时候，我们就知道了。

199
00:07:29.550 --> 00:07:35.050
So when it premiered, there was a lot of press about this being our last season.
所以当它首播时，有很多关于这是我们最后一季的媒体报道。

200
00:07:35.330 --> 00:07:36.890
But at this point,
但在此时此刻，

201
00:07:37.330 --> 00:07:51.030
what we knew was that Rain had only signed up to do 13 episodes of season nine because he and Paul Lieberstein were branching out and developing a spinoff of The Office called The Farm featuring Dwight.
我们当时知道的是，雷恩只签了第九季13集的合约，因为他和保罗·利伯斯坦正准备拓展业务，开发一部以德怀特为主角的《办公室》衍生剧《农场》。

202
00:07:51.030 --> 00:07:55.870
Yes, and this is why Paul stepped down as showrunner and Greg stepped back in.
没错，这就是为什么保罗辞去了剧集主管的职务，而格雷格又重新接手的原因。

203
00:07:56.430 --> 00:08:06.610
The idea was that Rainn Wilson would do a half season of The Office and then The Farm would come out in January and then Rainn would leave The Office, do The Farm,
当时的构想是让雷恩·威尔森出演半季《办公室》，然后《农场》在一月份开播，接着雷恩离开《办公室》去拍《农场》，

204
00:08:06.730 --> 00:08:08.130
and the two shows would overlap.
两部剧会有所重叠。

205
00:08:08.650 --> 00:08:16.650
Another thing that we knew was that Ed Helms only signed up to do a half a year because he was going to leave in the middle to shoot The Hangover 3.
我们还知道，艾德·赫尔姆斯也只签了半年的合约，因为他中间要离开去拍《宿醉3》。

206
00:08:17.150 --> 00:08:21.390
So we knew we would have Ed for a few episodes at the beginning and then a few at the end.
所以我们知道艾德在季初和季末会出演几集。

207
00:08:21.590 --> 00:08:26.710
So the only sort of two like quote unquote lead characters that were left were me and John.
因此，剩下的所谓“主角”就只有我和约翰了。

208
00:08:27.410 --> 00:08:36.510
And John wanted to do one more full year, but it kind of seemed like after that, we weren't sure if he was going to be up for a season 10.
约翰本来想再拍完整的一年，但看起来在那之后，我们不确定他是否还愿意拍第十季。

209
00:08:36.510 --> 00:08:41.350
And I wasn't really sure how Pam was going to stay on The Office without Jim.
而且我真的不知道如果没有吉姆，帕姆该如何在《办公室》里待下去。

210
00:08:41.750 --> 00:08:48.510
I was open to hearing options, but it did kind of seem like this was going to be Jim and Pam's last year all together.
我当时对各种选择持开放态度，但看起来这确实会是吉姆和帕姆在一起的最后一年了。

211
00:08:48.850 --> 00:08:50.070
Yes, at Dunder Mifflin.
没错，在邓德·米夫林公司。

212
00:08:50.150 --> 00:08:50.450
Yes.
是的。

213
00:08:50.450 --> 00:08:52.330
So as a result,
所以结果就是，

214
00:08:52.650 --> 00:09:02.210
they asked John and I to come on this season as producers so that we could help direct the Jim and Pam storyline since it was going to be our last full year together on the show.
他们邀请我和约翰在这一季担任制片人，这样我们就能协助指导吉姆和帕姆的故事线，因为这将是我们在一起拍戏的最后一个完整年度。

215
00:09:02.370 --> 00:09:11.470
And I have to applaud my BFF because all of a sudden this meant that you were going to have information that you couldn't share right away with me because you were now our producer.
我必须为我的好闺蜜鼓掌，因为这意味着你突然掌握了一些不能立刻告诉我的信息，因为你现在是我们的制片人了。

216
00:09:11.870 --> 00:09:13.330
You were very professional.
你表现得非常专业。

217
00:09:13.970 --> 00:09:18.470
You never spilled the beans on anything, even though I'm sure you wanted to.
你从来没有泄露过任何消息，尽管我肯定你当时很想说。

218
00:09:18.470 --> 00:09:21.170
You, so professional BFF.
你真是个专业的闺蜜。

219
00:09:21.690 --> 00:09:22.710
Thank you very much.
非常感谢。

220
00:09:22.770 --> 00:09:24.390
It was actually very difficult.
其实这真的很难。

221
00:09:24.550 --> 00:09:25.430
I know it was.
我知道很难。

222
00:09:26.150 --> 00:09:28.850
And I tried not to bug you because I knew it was hard.
我尽量不去烦你，因为我知道这不容易。

223
00:09:28.970 --> 00:09:30.750
And I appreciate that, Angela.
我很感激这一点，安吉拉。

224
00:09:31.470 --> 00:09:38.470
Well, like I said, by the time the season was ready to premiere, we all knew it would be our last season and we did tons of press and interviews about it.
嗯，就像我说的，当这一季准备首播时，我们都知道这将是最后一季，我们为此做了大量的宣传和采访。

225
00:09:38.630 --> 00:09:41.730
You can see all of them on officetelly.com.
你可以在officetelly.com上看到所有这些内容。

226
00:09:42.110 --> 00:09:43.550
Angela, we are all so emotional.
安吉拉，我们都太感性了。

227
00:09:43.830 --> 00:09:44.130
I know.
我知道。

228
00:09:44.250 --> 00:09:44.870
I watched a few.
我看了几个。

229
00:09:45.070 --> 00:09:46.390
We're all very weepy.
我们都哭得稀里哗啦的。

230
00:09:47.130 --> 00:09:50.710
Phyllis is like choking back tears the entire time she's being interviewed.
菲利斯在接受采访时全程都在强忍泪水。

231
00:09:50.970 --> 00:10:01.010
And I feel like if you want to truly understand how emotional we all were, you just have to listen to Creed's interview because he does not make a single joke in the interview.
我觉得如果你想真正了解我们当时有多感性，你只需要听听克里德的采访，因为他在采访中一个笑话都没讲。

232
00:10:01.970 --> 00:10:03.010
He's totally serious.
他非常严肃。

233
00:10:03.190 --> 00:10:04.130
I have the audio clip.
我有那段音频片段。

234
00:10:04.170 --> 00:10:04.930
Let's hear it.
让我们听听看。

235
00:10:05.730 --> 00:10:18.070
I think we want to go out with a bang and raise our game and walk out of here feeling like we've, well, we already feel like we've been on a winning show and we've left a mark.
我想我们想以精彩的方式收尾，提升我们的表现，离开时感觉我们，嗯，我们已经觉得我们参与了一部成功的剧集，并且留下了自己的印记。

236
00:10:18.070 --> 00:10:22.750
And, but obviously you want to take it up, take up the, take the bar, raise the bar a little bit higher.
而且，显然你想更进一步，把标准再提高一点。

237
00:10:22.970 --> 00:10:34.430
So I think we're all pulling together as a team and not that we always haven't, but yeah, it's, it's kind of, I wouldn't say I'm not modeling about it, but it's been,
所以我认为我们都在齐心协力，并不是说我们以前没有这样做过，但确实，这有点，我不会说我对此感到伤感，但它已经，

238
00:10:34.590 --> 00:10:38.590
it's this family, you know, it's going to be, it's going to be sad leaving these people.
这就像一个大家庭，你知道，离开这些人会让人很难过。

239
00:10:38.590 --> 00:10:39.330
Right.
没错。

240
00:10:41.020 --> 00:10:41.480
Oh yeah.
哦，是的。

241
00:10:41.820 --> 00:10:41.980
Right.
没错。

242
00:10:42.280 --> 00:10:48.100
Because Creed normally cuts stuff with a joke, you know, but that was just so honest and.
因为克里德通常会用笑话来结束话题，你知道，但那段话真的很真诚，而且。

243
00:10:48.240 --> 00:10:48.500
Yeah.
是啊。

244
00:10:48.800 --> 00:10:49.020
Yeah.
没错。

245
00:10:49.220 --> 00:10:53.520
And I felt like it kind of summed up perfectly how we felt about it.
我觉得它完美地总结了我们当时的心情。

246
00:10:53.740 --> 00:10:53.940
Yeah.
是啊。

247
00:10:54.180 --> 00:10:54.460
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

248
00:10:55.120 --> 00:10:57.260
Are you ready for fast fact number two?
准备好听第二个快速事实了吗？

249
00:10:57.560 --> 00:10:58.020
I am.
准备好了。

250
00:10:58.080 --> 00:11:01.720
I'm just like, oh my gosh, am I going to be weepy this whole last season nine?
我只是觉得，天哪，难道我整个第九季最后一季都要泪流满面吗？

251
00:11:01.920 --> 00:11:02.300
Maybe.
也许吧。

252
00:11:02.560 --> 00:11:02.800
Maybe.
也许吧。

253
00:11:03.100 --> 00:11:03.380
Okay.
好吧。

254
00:11:03.760 --> 00:11:08.660
Well, fast fact number two is all about finding our new guys, Clark and Pete.
好了，第二个速览事实是关于我们如何找到新人的，也就是克拉克和皮特。

255
00:11:08.660 --> 00:11:09.600
Yes, R.
没错，R。

256
00:11:09.680 --> 00:11:13.880
Plop and Dwight Jr., who could have been called fart, but.
“噗噗”和“小德怀特”，本来可以叫“屁屁”的，但是。

257
00:11:14.060 --> 00:11:15.560
No, went another way.
没有，选了别的名字。

258
00:11:15.800 --> 00:11:16.280
Went another way.
选了别的名字。

259
00:11:16.480 --> 00:11:18.140
Well, we got a lot of fan mail.
我们收到了很多粉丝来信。

260
00:11:18.700 --> 00:11:24.640
Corey Kaye from Illinois said, please tell us everything about the actors who played Clark and Plop.
来自伊利诺伊州的科里·凯说，请告诉我们关于饰演克拉克和“噗噗”的演员的一切。

261
00:11:24.920 --> 00:11:26.820
Love these two additions to The Office.
很喜欢《办公室》里这两个新角色。

262
00:11:27.160 --> 00:11:27.820
And Jamie D.
还有来自佐治亚州亚特兰大的杰米·D。

263
00:11:28.040 --> 00:11:35.900
from Atlanta, Georgia said, I love the addition of Clark and Plop, especially Clark, who is in my top three favorite Office characters.
说，我喜欢克拉克和“噗噗”的加入，尤其是克拉克，他是我最喜欢的《办公室》角色前三名。

264
00:11:35.900 --> 00:11:38.200
And I want to know everything about how he came to be.
我想知道关于他如何加入剧组的一切。

265
00:11:38.500 --> 00:11:40.580
Give me the deets, please, and thank you.
请给我详细信息，谢谢。

266
00:11:40.740 --> 00:11:45.740
Well, I reached out to our casting director, Allison Jones, to find out what exactly happened.
我联系了我们的选角导演艾莉森·琼斯，想弄清楚到底发生了什么。

267
00:11:45.740 --> 00:11:47.220
How did we find these guys?
我们是怎么找到这些人的？

268
00:11:48.120 --> 00:11:51.600
Allison said this was an extensive search.
艾莉森说这是一次大规模的搜寻。

269
00:11:52.360 --> 00:11:59.380
She said not since she had to cast the role of Karen has she auditioned so many people for a role in The Office.
她说自从为《办公室》选凯伦这个角色以来，她还没为哪个角色试镜过这么多人。

270
00:11:59.380 --> 00:12:04.560
I bet two new people coming in at this stage in the show.
我敢说，在剧集这个阶段引入两个新人确实不容易。

271
00:12:04.780 --> 00:12:06.780
She said she auditioned people in New York.
她说她在纽约试镜了很多人。

272
00:12:06.780 --> 00:12:08.500
She auditioned people in Los Angeles.
她在洛杉矶也试镜了很多人。

273
00:12:08.800 --> 00:12:19.180
And one of the reasons that they searched so intensely to cast these two actors was because at this point, there was an idea that The Office would continue into season 10.
他们之所以如此费力地寻找这两位演员，原因之一是当时有一种想法，认为《办公室》会继续拍到第十季。

274
00:12:20.100 --> 00:12:30.480
Even if some of the regular cast members moved on, the idea was that these two new people were going to move us into the next generation of The Office.
即使一些常规演员离开，他们的想法是这两个新人将带领我们进入《办公室》的下一代。

275
00:12:31.520 --> 00:12:42.200
And Clark Duke did an interview where he said, when Jake and I joined the show, the idea was that this was going to be a show like ER, where new leads could move in and out,
克拉克·杜克在一次采访中说，当我和杰克加入剧组时，大家的想法是这会像《急诊室的故事》那样，新的主角可以来来去去，

276
00:12:42.260 --> 00:12:44.280
and it might run for like 20 years.
而且可能会播个20年左右。

277
00:12:44.280 --> 00:12:46.000
So that was the vision.
这就是当时的愿景。

278
00:12:46.300 --> 00:12:50.120
Allison wasn't just casting like guest stars or recurring characters.
艾莉森不仅仅是在选客串明星或常驻角色。

279
00:12:50.340 --> 00:12:52.940
She was casting the next phase of The Office.
她是在选《办公室》的下一阶段人选。

280
00:12:53.220 --> 00:12:54.440
The comedy ER.
喜剧版的《急诊室的故事》。

281
00:12:54.780 --> 00:12:55.200
Yes.
没错。

282
00:12:55.260 --> 00:13:02.040
The 20 years in Dunder Mifflin just rotating people through this paper company.
在邓德·米夫林公司工作20年，人员不断轮换。

283
00:13:02.160 --> 00:13:02.760
That's right.
没错。

284
00:13:03.120 --> 00:13:06.540
The most successful small paper company.
最成功的小型造纸公司。

285
00:13:07.220 --> 00:13:09.560
With a documentary that never ends.
还有一部永远拍不完的纪录片。

286
00:13:09.560 --> 00:13:10.440
Never ends.
永远拍不完。

287
00:13:10.440 --> 00:13:14.700
Well, Allison knew Clark Duke, who was cast as Clark.
艾莉森认识饰演克拉克的克拉克·杜克。

288
00:13:15.040 --> 00:13:16.320
He was cast firSt.
他最先被选中。

289
00:13:16.680 --> 00:13:20.700
He had done a show called Clark and Michael, starring himself and Michael Cera.
他曾出演过一部名为《克拉克与迈克尔》的剧，由他和迈克尔·塞拉主演。

290
00:13:20.900 --> 00:13:25.200
He was also in Hot Tub Time Machine with Craig Robinson and Kick-Ass.
他还和克雷格·罗宾逊一起演过《热浴盆时光机》，还演过《海扁王》。

291
00:13:25.320 --> 00:13:28.940
He was sort of in that Judd Apatow comedy circle.
他算是贾德·阿帕图那个喜剧圈子里的人。

292
00:13:29.740 --> 00:13:33.920
Allison thinks that he did not even audition, that they offered him the role.
艾莉森认为他甚至没有参加试镜，他们直接给了他这个角色。

293
00:13:34.420 --> 00:13:36.560
So they got that done firSt.
所以这件事最先搞定了。

294
00:13:37.000 --> 00:13:40.560
And I found an audio clip of Clark talking about joining the show.
我找到了一段克拉克谈论加入剧组的音频片段。

295
00:13:40.680 --> 00:13:41.460
Would you like to hear it?
你想听听吗？

296
00:13:41.560 --> 00:13:41.960
Yes.
想。

297
00:13:42.940 --> 00:13:46.040
I was really flattered when they approached me about it.
当他们找我谈这件事时，我真的受宠若惊。

298
00:13:46.160 --> 00:13:51.080
I'm a big fan of the show and have been since it started, I guess, nine years ago.
我是这部剧的忠实粉丝，我想从九年前开播起就是了。

299
00:13:51.380 --> 00:13:52.860
And the British one before that.
在那之前还看过英版。

300
00:13:53.040 --> 00:13:55.560
So I was very excited, thrilled to be a part of it.
所以我非常兴奋，能参与其中感到非常激动。

301
00:13:56.120 --> 00:14:03.580
My character is also named Clark, which is convenient, because it's easy to remember, you know, on the call sheet, too.
我的角色也叫克拉克，这很方便，因为记起来很容易，你知道，在通告单上也一样。

302
00:14:04.200 --> 00:14:07.960
You know, without giving it too much away, but there's really not, like, any big secrets.
你知道，虽然不能剧透太多，但其实也没什么大秘密。

303
00:14:07.960 --> 00:14:10.100
My guy is just sort of a new guy that works at the office.
我演的这个角色只是办公室里的一个新人。

304
00:14:10.420 --> 00:14:13.540
He's not, like, a secret agent or anything that's infiltrated the office.
他不是什么特工，也不是那种潜入办公室的人。

305
00:14:14.700 --> 00:14:15.560
So there you go.
所以就是这样。

306
00:14:15.560 --> 00:14:19.720
Well, I have two things to share about Clark and Jake.
嗯，关于克拉克和杰克，我有两件事要分享。

307
00:14:20.160 --> 00:14:28.140
So since you're talking about Clark, we got into this conversation one day on set because his last name is Duke.
既然你在说克拉克，有一天我们在片场聊到了这个话题，因为他的姓是杜克。

308
00:14:28.760 --> 00:14:30.920
And my mom's maiden name is Duke.
而我妈妈的娘家姓也是杜克。

309
00:14:31.100 --> 00:14:32.900
And I was like, Clark, what if we're related?
我就说，克拉克，万一我们有亲戚关系呢？

310
00:14:33.720 --> 00:14:36.420
And so then we started trying to figure it out.
于是我们就开始试着查清楚。

311
00:14:36.520 --> 00:14:38.980
And he talked to his mom and I talked to my mom.
他去问了他妈妈，我也问了我妈妈。

312
00:14:39.100 --> 00:14:42.060
And we're like, my mom was like, well, we did have some family that moved around.
我们当时就像，我妈说，嗯，我们确实有些亲戚搬来搬去过。

313
00:14:42.060 --> 00:14:45.500
And so we sort of joked that we were maybe distant cousins.
所以我们就开玩笑说，也许我们是远房表亲。

314
00:14:46.280 --> 00:14:47.960
But you never found out for sure?
但你们一直没查出个确切结果？

315
00:14:48.200 --> 00:14:49.140
We never found out for sure.
我们一直没查出个确切结果。

316
00:14:49.360 --> 00:14:52.220
But I did start sending his family my Christmas card.
但我确实开始给他的家人寄我的圣诞贺卡了。

317
00:14:52.720 --> 00:14:53.620
Just in case.
以防万一。

318
00:14:53.620 --> 00:14:54.380
Just in case.
以防万一。

319
00:14:54.440 --> 00:14:57.000
And his mom would send me their Christmas card.
他妈妈也会给我寄他们的圣诞贺卡。

320
00:14:57.120 --> 00:14:58.320
That is the sweetest thing.
这真是太贴心了。

321
00:14:58.340 --> 00:14:59.200
I just love that.
我太喜欢这个了。

322
00:15:00.360 --> 00:15:04.860
Well, let's move on to Jake Lacey now, who got the role of Pete.
好了，现在我们来聊聊杰克·莱西，他得到了皮特这个角色。

323
00:15:05.380 --> 00:15:08.760
Allison said that they read a couple hundred people for the role of Pete.
艾莉森说他们为皮特这个角色面试了几百人。

324
00:15:09.060 --> 00:15:11.460
And eventually they settled on a handful of people.
最终他们选定了几个人。

325
00:15:11.880 --> 00:15:14.920
They flew Jake in from New York to meet with Greg.
他们把杰克从纽约飞过来见格雷格。

326
00:15:15.280 --> 00:15:19.220
And Jake did not have a lot of TV credits when he got the role in The Office.
杰克在得到《办公室》的角色时，并没有太多的电视作品。

327
00:15:19.440 --> 00:15:21.600
He basically just killed it in his audition.
他基本上就是在试镜时表现得太棒了。

328
00:15:21.760 --> 00:15:22.860
That is how he got the role.
这就是他得到角色的原因。

329
00:15:23.100 --> 00:15:26.980
By the way, not having a lot of TV credits with Greg doesn't mean anything.
顺便说一下，在格雷格看来，没有太多电视作品根本不算什么。

330
00:15:27.260 --> 00:15:27.600
No.
没错。

331
00:15:27.920 --> 00:15:31.140
That was the wonderful thing about all of us getting cast on The Office.
这就是我们所有人能被选入《办公室》最棒的地方。

332
00:15:31.480 --> 00:15:34.180
He was like, I don't care about your experience.
他当时的态度是，我不在乎你的经验。

333
00:15:34.180 --> 00:15:35.100
Are you great?
你够优秀吗？

334
00:15:35.460 --> 00:15:35.600
Yeah.
是的。

335
00:15:36.080 --> 00:15:36.380
Done.
行。

336
00:15:36.640 --> 00:15:37.460
You get the job.
这工作归你了。

337
00:15:37.460 --> 00:15:46.320
Jake did an interview at the start of the season where he said he had started watching The Office when he was in college and he was a huge fan of the show.
杰克在这一季开始时接受过一次采访，他说他在大学时就开始看《办公室》了，而且是这部剧的超级粉丝。

338
00:15:46.660 --> 00:15:48.260
And I remember this, Angela.
我记得这件事，安吉拉。

339
00:15:48.560 --> 00:15:49.540
I remember talking about this.
我记得我们聊过这个。

340
00:15:49.620 --> 00:15:51.120
It made me feel very old on set.
这让我在片场感觉自己老了很多。

341
00:15:51.240 --> 00:15:52.980
But here's the audio clip.
但这里有一段音频片段。

342
00:15:53.920 --> 00:15:55.900
Yeah, this was definitely my dream job.
是的，这绝对是我梦寐以求的工作。

343
00:15:56.120 --> 00:16:03.480
I think, you know, three months ago if you had said, there's any show, you pick it, you can be on it, I would have said The Office.
我想，你知道，如果三个月前你问我，有哪部剧，你随便挑，你可以去演，我会说是《办公室》。

344
00:16:05.320 --> 00:16:13.300
And I was just blown away when this opportunity came up and then to get out here and test for it and think like, wow, it's getting close, you know.
当这个机会出现时，我简直惊呆了，然后来到这里试镜，心想，哇，离梦想成真越来越近了，你知道的。

345
00:16:13.460 --> 00:16:17.700
And then to find out that I got it was thrilling, absolutely thrilling.
后来得知我被选上了，真是太令人激动了，绝对令人激动。

346
00:16:19.000 --> 00:16:21.480
I mean, yeah, they were so young.
我是说，没错，他们太年轻了。

347
00:16:21.600 --> 00:16:22.300
We were dinosaurs.
我们简直是老古董了。

348
00:16:22.640 --> 00:16:24.420
I remember feeling very old around them.
我记得在他们身边感觉自己特别老。

349
00:16:24.500 --> 00:16:24.900
Me too.
我也是。

350
00:16:25.340 --> 00:16:26.440
I loved them.
我喜欢他们。

351
00:16:26.600 --> 00:16:27.040
I know.
我知道。

352
00:16:27.160 --> 00:16:27.840
They were wonderful.
他们太棒了。

353
00:16:28.020 --> 00:16:28.500
And you know what?
而且你知道吗？

354
00:16:28.580 --> 00:16:30.780
They were this really fun new energy.
他们带来了一种非常有趣的新活力。

355
00:16:31.000 --> 00:16:32.380
They were the new guys.
他们是新人。

356
00:16:32.420 --> 00:16:32.860
They were.
确实如此。

357
00:16:33.100 --> 00:16:35.180
It was great having them around.
有他们在身边感觉真好。

358
00:16:35.440 --> 00:16:37.480
Here's my little thing about Jake Lacey.
关于杰克·莱西，我有个小故事。

359
00:16:37.940 --> 00:16:40.520
I was walking down the hallway to the set.
当时我正沿着走廊走向片场。

360
00:16:40.680 --> 00:16:44.840
We had this sort of area behind the set we've talked about where hair and makeup was.
我们在片场后面有个区域，之前提到过，那是化妆和发型间所在的地方。

361
00:16:44.840 --> 00:16:50.560
And you would walk down this little corridor and then all of a sudden you were in the bullpen of Dundra Mifflin.
你得穿过那条小走廊，然后突然就到了邓德·米夫林的办公区。

362
00:16:50.900 --> 00:16:55.220
And I'm walking down this corridor and I hear this voice behind me talking to someone.
我走在走廊里，听到身后有个声音在跟人说话。

363
00:16:55.400 --> 00:16:58.220
And I thought, oh, Jenna's husband Lee is on set today.
我心想，哦，珍娜的丈夫李今天在片场。

364
00:16:58.760 --> 00:17:02.000
And I turned, I literally, I think I said Lee as I turned around.
我转过身，我记得我转身时甚至直接喊了声李。

365
00:17:02.120 --> 00:17:03.120
I think I was like, Lee?
我当时好像说了句，李？

366
00:17:03.500 --> 00:17:04.700
And it was Jake.
结果是杰克。

367
00:17:05.820 --> 00:17:09.140
I thought he sounded so similar to your husband.
我觉得他的声音和你丈夫太像了。

368
00:17:09.540 --> 00:17:14.440
His voice is, the cadence, something about it is so similar that it would just throw me off.
他的嗓音、说话的节奏，有种说不出的相似感，总是让我产生错觉。

369
00:17:14.440 --> 00:17:19.700
The first big conference room scenes we would have, I'd be like, I keep thinking Lee is here.
我们第一次拍大型会议室场景时，我心想，我怎么老觉得李在这里。

370
00:17:20.640 --> 00:17:21.720
That's so funny.
太搞笑了。

371
00:17:21.740 --> 00:17:23.260
I remember you telling me that.
我记得你跟我说过这个。

372
00:17:23.380 --> 00:17:24.120
And I hear it.
我听得出来。

373
00:17:24.240 --> 00:17:25.160
I can hear it.
我能听出那种相似感。

374
00:17:25.440 --> 00:17:27.680
Well, we will have more stories about these guys.
好吧，以后我们会有更多关于他们的故事。

375
00:17:27.820 --> 00:17:30.280
And obviously, we're going to ask them to come on Office Lady.
显然，我们要邀请他们来上《办公室女士》节目。

376
00:17:30.560 --> 00:17:30.800
Yes.
没错。

377
00:17:30.980 --> 00:17:32.660
Jake and Clark, you have to come on.
杰克和克拉克，你们一定要来。

378
00:17:33.300 --> 00:17:37.240
Now, fast fact number three is a fan question from Elsa S.
现在，第三个速记事实是来自明尼苏达州艾尔莎·S的粉丝提问，

379
00:17:37.540 --> 00:17:39.300
in Minnesota who asked,
她问道，

380
00:17:39.760 --> 00:17:45.880
this episode is the first time we see a big shift in Andy's personality that continues for the rest of season nine.
这一集是安迪性格发生重大转变的开始，这种转变一直持续到第九季结束。

381
00:17:46.340 --> 00:17:46.420
Elsa.
艾尔莎。

382
00:17:46.860 --> 00:17:47.820
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

383
00:17:48.340 --> 00:17:50.340
Elsa, I have so many thoughts on this.
艾尔莎，我对此有很多想法。

384
00:17:50.440 --> 00:17:51.420
I'm so glad you wrote in.
很高兴你写信来问。

385
00:17:51.560 --> 00:17:52.720
Sorry, Jenna, I interrupted you.
抱歉，珍娜，我打断你了。

386
00:17:52.780 --> 00:17:53.080
Go on.
你继续。

387
00:17:53.160 --> 00:17:53.520
No, no.
不，没事。

388
00:17:53.660 --> 00:17:59.400
Elsa went on to say he has always had flaws, but generally been a likable guy until now.
艾尔莎接着说，他一直都有缺点，但直到现在总体上还是个讨人喜欢的家伙。

389
00:17:59.880 --> 00:18:03.760
Do you have any insights into why the writers chose to make this change?
你对编剧们为何选择做出这种改变有什么见解吗？

390
00:18:03.760 --> 00:18:08.500
Well, clearly, from what you shared, he was going to be leaving the show.
嗯，很明显，从你分享的内容来看，他当时要离开剧组了。

391
00:18:08.680 --> 00:18:14.260
But my thought is, like, I imagine this writers room meeting, which I know didn't happen, where they're like,
但我的想法是，我能想象出那个编剧会议——虽然我知道没发生过——他们当时在想，

392
00:18:14.420 --> 00:18:16.460
how do we just burn Andy to the ground?
我们该怎么彻底毁掉安迪这个角色？

393
00:18:16.620 --> 00:18:17.160
I know.
我知道。

394
00:18:17.540 --> 00:18:19.680
How do we make him so horrible?
我们该怎么让他变得那么糟糕？

395
00:18:20.660 --> 00:18:25.560
Well, I traded emails with Greg Daniels about this episode, and he said yes.
嗯，我曾就这一集和格雷格·丹尼尔斯通过邮件，他说确实如此。

396
00:18:25.840 --> 00:18:30.100
They knew that Ed was going to be missing for a big chunk of episodes in the middle of the season,
他们知道艾德在季中会有很大一部分剧集缺席，

397
00:18:30.100 --> 00:18:32.100
and they had to write toward that.
所以他们必须围绕这一点来创作。

398
00:18:32.100 --> 00:18:35.220
They had to come up with a reason why he was going to disappear.
他们必须想出一个他会消失的理由。

399
00:18:35.540 --> 00:18:38.540
So that kind of started from there, and they worked backwards.
所以一切就是从那里开始的，他们进行了倒推。

400
00:18:39.000 --> 00:18:42.300
But in the writers room, they talked about who is Andy.
但在编剧室里，他们讨论过安迪到底是个什么样的人。

401
00:18:42.640 --> 00:18:48.980
And Greg said he was originally a guy with anger management issues who put his fists through a wall.
格雷格说他最初是个有愤怒管理问题的人，曾一拳砸穿过墙壁。

402
00:18:49.560 --> 00:18:57.280
And over in Stanford, he had been introduced as kind of like an antagonistic, Dwight-like, annoying deskmate for Jim.
而在斯坦福那边，他被设定为吉姆那种充满敌意、像德怀特一样烦人的同桌。

403
00:18:57.560 --> 00:19:00.620
And they wanted to bring back some of the old qualities of the character.
他们想找回这个角色身上的一些旧特质。

404
00:19:00.620 --> 00:19:14.060
They said they actually feel like the Andy we're seeing in season nine is a truer extension of where Andy started than the softer character that we've been seeing for the last season.
他们说，其实他们觉得第九季里的安迪，比我们上一季看到的那个温和的角色，更像是安迪最初设定的延伸。

405
00:19:14.280 --> 00:19:17.640
He said, you know, Andy wasn't designed to be the lead of a show.
他说，你知道的，安迪并不是为了当主角而设计的。

406
00:19:17.840 --> 00:19:19.720
He was designed to be a flavor.
他被设计成一种调味剂。

407
00:19:19.720 --> 00:19:23.260
And they wanted to bring that flavor back to the show.
他们想把那种调味剂带回剧中。

408
00:19:23.800 --> 00:19:28.520
Greg also said that this version of Andy was more capable of foolishness.
格雷格还说，这个版本的安迪更能折腾出蠢事来。

409
00:19:29.040 --> 00:19:29.860
Foolishness-ness.
愚蠢感。

410
00:19:30.340 --> 00:19:30.900
Foolishness.
愚蠢。

411
00:19:31.060 --> 00:19:31.620
Foolishness.
愚蠢。

412
00:19:31.980 --> 00:19:32.740
Foolishness-ness.
愚蠢感。

413
00:19:32.980 --> 00:19:33.380
I don't know.
我不知道。

414
00:19:33.460 --> 00:19:34.820
That's ultimate foolishness.
那是极致的愚蠢。

415
00:19:35.300 --> 00:19:36.500
If you're foolishness-ness.
如果你有愚蠢感的话。

416
00:19:36.700 --> 00:19:37.480
It's ultimate.
这是极致的。

417
00:19:37.660 --> 00:19:38.180
It's ultimate.
这是极致的。

418
00:19:39.060 --> 00:19:45.860
Finally, Greg said that this change in Andy's character was also going to help kind of serve his vision,
最后，格雷格说安迪这个角色的转变也有助于实现他的构想，

419
00:19:46.160 --> 00:19:55.620
which was to center the season around Jim and Pam and Dwight and Angela as our core characters and follow their relationships through.
那就是让这一季围绕吉姆、帕姆、德怀特和安吉拉这几个核心角色展开，并深入刻画他们的关系。

420
00:19:56.140 --> 00:19:57.800
Well, Ange, that's all I got.
好了，安吉，我说的就这些。

421
00:19:57.940 --> 00:19:59.920
That was a long top of show today.
今天开场的内容真长啊。

422
00:20:00.300 --> 00:20:01.540
Yeah, you had a lot of stuff.
是啊，你准备的内容真不少。

423
00:20:01.720 --> 00:20:02.580
I loved it all.
我全都很喜欢。

424
00:20:02.660 --> 00:20:03.440
A new season?
新的一季？

425
00:20:03.440 --> 00:20:04.520
It's a new year.
是新的一年。

426
00:20:04.520 --> 00:20:05.080
Yes.
没错。

427
00:20:05.500 --> 00:20:09.300
Well, I have quite a bit for this episode from my digital clutter.
好吧，我从我的数字杂物里整理出不少关于这一集的内容。

428
00:20:10.000 --> 00:20:11.640
I have call sheets.
我有通告单。

429
00:20:12.020 --> 00:20:12.420
Ooh.
噢。

430
00:20:13.260 --> 00:20:14.560
But why don't we take a break?
但我们为什么不先休息一下呢？

431
00:20:14.560 --> 00:20:16.700
Because when we come back, we'll get into this episode.
因为回来之后，我们就要进入这一集的内容了。

432
00:20:17.400 --> 00:20:21.020
I have a lot of questions about Erin's new hairdo.
我对艾琳的新发型有很多疑问。

433
00:20:21.500 --> 00:20:21.940
Oh.
噢。

434
00:20:22.160 --> 00:20:23.280
To kick things off.
先从这个说起吧。

435
00:20:23.420 --> 00:20:23.680
Okay.
好的。

436
00:20:35.290 --> 00:20:36.390
Well, we are back.
好了，我们回来了。

437
00:20:36.650 --> 00:20:37.410
Erin is at work.
艾琳在上班。

438
00:20:37.510 --> 00:20:40.010
She's very excited because Andy's coming back today.
她非常兴奋，因为安迪今天就要回来了。

439
00:20:40.230 --> 00:20:41.290
Andy's coming back today.
安迪今天就要回来了。

440
00:20:41.450 --> 00:20:41.850
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

441
00:20:42.310 --> 00:20:43.430
Nellie's not so excited.
奈莉可没那么兴奋。

442
00:20:43.750 --> 00:20:44.910
Why is she nervous?
她为什么紧张？

443
00:20:44.910 --> 00:20:54.210
I mean, I'm going to have to say that as we go through the very top of this episode, I have some continuity things that don't quite line up.
我是说，我得提一下，当我们回顾这一集的开头时，我发现有些连贯性上的问题对不上。

444
00:20:54.650 --> 00:20:55.790
I'm going to bring them up.
我会把它们提出来。

445
00:20:55.850 --> 00:21:02.170
And the first one is, why is Nellie nervous about Andy's return if we don't know that he's a total jerk yet?
第一个问题是，如果我们还不知道安迪是个彻头彻尾的混蛋，那奈莉为什么会因为他的回归而紧张？

446
00:21:02.490 --> 00:21:02.670
Right.
对啊。

447
00:21:02.890 --> 00:21:05.710
Did something happen we didn't see before he left?
在他离开之前，是不是发生了什么我们没看到的事？

448
00:21:05.930 --> 00:21:10.490
I might have a few things from the shooting draft that might help, but not really.
我手头或许有一些拍摄初稿的内容能帮上忙，但其实也没什么用。

449
00:21:10.650 --> 00:21:12.210
There's just some continuity holes.
这纯粹就是一些连贯性上的漏洞。

450
00:21:12.410 --> 00:21:12.670
Yeah.
