00:27:58.270 --> 00:27:58.450
Yeah.
没错。

610
00:27:58.450 --> 00:28:03.030
And then Dwight is going to vomit his beet energy drink all over Angela.
然后德怀特会把他的甜菜能量饮料吐得安吉拉满身都是。

611
00:28:03.490 --> 00:28:04.650
All over.
全身都是。

612
00:28:05.150 --> 00:28:07.130
Fan catch from Jenna F.
来自洛杉矶加利福尼亚州的珍娜·F的粉丝提问。

613
00:28:07.290 --> 00:28:08.810
in Los Angeles, California.
在加利福尼亚州洛杉矶。

614
00:28:08.970 --> 00:28:10.690
Jenna wrote in a lot for this episode.
珍娜为这一集写了很多内容。

615
00:28:10.870 --> 00:28:11.610
Yes, she did.
是的，她写了。

616
00:28:12.070 --> 00:28:15.730
Dwight says he started making his beet runoff juice over the summer.
德怀特说他从夏天开始制作他的甜菜汁。

617
00:28:15.950 --> 00:28:16.190
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

618
00:28:16.190 --> 00:28:20.690
So how did he vomit it all over Angela at the hospital, which was before the summer?
那他怎么会在医院里把它吐得安吉拉满身都是呢，那可是夏天之前的事？

619
00:28:20.870 --> 00:28:21.110
Yes.
没错。

620
00:28:21.110 --> 00:28:23.250
This was not explained in the shooting draft.
拍摄剧本里没有解释这一点。

621
00:28:24.270 --> 00:28:28.150
And now, Angela, fan question from Valeria in Italy.
现在，安吉拉，来自意大利瓦莱里娅的粉丝提问。

622
00:28:28.930 --> 00:28:33.130
Obviously, I need to know how Angela and Rain shot the vomit scene.
显然，我需要知道安吉拉和雷恩是怎么拍摄呕吐那场戏的。

623
00:28:33.130 --> 00:28:37.430
I can clearly see that some of the stuff went into Angela's mouth.
我清楚地看到有些东西进了安吉拉的嘴里。

624
00:28:37.750 --> 00:28:38.310
Okay.
好的。

625
00:28:38.310 --> 00:28:39.730
I have all the details.
我有所有细节。

626
00:28:40.010 --> 00:28:40.210
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

627
00:28:40.230 --> 00:28:44.890
First of all, the reason I have a ponytail is because they were worried this stuff was going
首先，我扎马尾辫的原因是他们担心这些东西会

628
00:28:44.890 --> 00:28:48.170
to get in my hair, and we wouldn't be able to reset as quickly.
弄到我的头发上，那样我们就没法快速重拍了。

629
00:28:48.510 --> 00:28:48.950
Okay.
好的。

630
00:28:49.390 --> 00:28:49.690
Right?
对吧？

631
00:28:49.950 --> 00:28:50.250
So.
所以。

632
00:28:50.250 --> 00:28:53.950
Because that would mean washing my hair, blow drying my hair, flat ironing my hair.
因为那意味着要洗头、吹干头发、用直发夹板拉直头发。

633
00:28:54.130 --> 00:28:55.910
You can't do that in between takes.
在拍摄间隙你没法做这些。

634
00:28:57.150 --> 00:28:58.770
So that's why the ponytail.
所以这就是扎马尾辫的原因。

635
00:28:59.270 --> 00:28:59.590
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

636
00:28:59.850 --> 00:29:01.630
Secondly, they made this.
其次，他们制作了这个东西。

637
00:29:01.770 --> 00:29:07.130
It looked like, you know, when people go hiking and they drink out of those, like, pouches of water
看起来就像，你知道，人们去徒步旅行时喝的那种水袋，

638
00:29:07.130 --> 00:29:10.610
and they have the little bendy straw they suck on.
上面有个小弯管可以吸水。

639
00:29:10.750 --> 00:29:12.110
Yeah, like camelback, right?
对，就像骆驼背水袋，对吧？

640
00:29:12.230 --> 00:29:13.430
Yes, that's it.
是的，就是那个。

641
00:29:13.670 --> 00:29:13.810
Yeah.
没错。

642
00:29:13.970 --> 00:29:19.610
They made one of these, and they sort of strapped it to rain under his blazer jacket.
他们做了一个这样的装置，把它绑在雷恩的西装外套下面。

643
00:29:19.950 --> 00:29:20.470
Really?
真的吗？

644
00:29:20.710 --> 00:29:28.310
So he turned to me when it was time to vomit and just kind of squirted this blue stuff all over me.
所以当需要呕吐的时候，他转向我，直接把这些蓝色液体喷了我一身。

645
00:29:28.430 --> 00:29:30.630
So it didn't really come out of his mouth.
所以它并不是真的从他嘴里吐出来的。

646
00:29:30.770 --> 00:29:31.290
No.
不是。

647
00:29:31.630 --> 00:29:31.870
No.
不是。

648
00:29:31.870 --> 00:29:33.710
I would have never guessed that.
我绝对猜不到。

649
00:29:33.710 --> 00:29:40.450
You really thought that rain, they had rain spit blue, like, hurl blue stuff at me out of his own mouth?
你真的以为雷恩，他们让雷恩吐出蓝色的东西，就像，从他自己嘴里喷出蓝色液体喷到我身上？

650
00:29:40.590 --> 00:29:40.990
Yes.
是的。

651
00:29:41.250 --> 00:29:41.510
No.
不。

652
00:29:41.670 --> 00:29:42.770
That's what it looked like to me.
我看起来就是那样。

653
00:29:42.850 --> 00:29:45.030
I would have never guessed that this was rigged.
我怎么也想不到这是做了手脚的。

654
00:29:45.090 --> 00:29:46.050
It looked so real.
看起来太真实了。

655
00:29:46.170 --> 00:29:47.310
No, it's, look at it.
不，你看，你看它。

656
00:29:47.330 --> 00:29:48.590
It looks so projectile.
看起来喷射感十足。

657
00:29:48.830 --> 00:29:49.230
I know.
我知道。

658
00:29:49.330 --> 00:29:50.850
I couldn't figure out how he did it.
我没法弄明白他是怎么做到的。

659
00:29:50.950 --> 00:29:55.390
It was a little, like, camelback thing that he squirted with the hose.
那是个像骆驼背一样的小玩意儿，他用软管往里面注水。

660
00:29:55.610 --> 00:29:57.030
He had, like, a little hose thing.
他有个类似小软管的东西。

661
00:29:57.270 --> 00:29:59.630
That's why he turned so much to the wall.
这就是为什么他转过身对着墙。

662
00:30:00.210 --> 00:30:02.110
But, yeah, it got all over me.
但是，没错，我身上全沾上了。

663
00:30:02.410 --> 00:30:03.370
Did it get in your mouth?
溅到你嘴里了吗？

664
00:30:03.370 --> 00:30:04.570
Some of it went in my mouth.
有些溅进我嘴里了。

665
00:30:04.730 --> 00:30:05.550
What did it taste like?
是什么味道？

666
00:30:05.550 --> 00:30:07.790
I do think it was, like, some kind of blue Gatorade.
我觉得那应该是某种蓝色佳得乐。

667
00:30:07.870 --> 00:30:08.490
I do.
我是这么觉得的。

668
00:30:08.630 --> 00:30:09.310
I can't remember.
我记不清了。

669
00:30:09.510 --> 00:30:10.510
It didn't taste horrible.
味道不算太糟糕。

670
00:30:10.670 --> 00:30:10.930
Okay.
好吧。

671
00:30:11.010 --> 00:30:11.590
I remember that.
我记得那个。

672
00:30:12.430 --> 00:30:20.730
And I have a photo backstage after our first take of this where I am doused with all this blue stuff.
我还有一张照片，是在我们拍完第一条后在后台拍的，当时我浑身都被那蓝色的东西淋透了。

673
00:30:20.830 --> 00:30:24.550
They had a second set of the wardrobe and a robe for me to change.
他们准备了第二套服装和一件长袍让我换。

674
00:30:24.790 --> 00:30:27.950
But I'm just standing in the hallway with, like, my arms out.
但我当时就站在走廊里，张开双臂。

675
00:30:27.950 --> 00:30:30.290
I'm just covered in this blue liquid.
我浑身都是那种蓝色液体。

676
00:30:30.850 --> 00:30:39.810
So, yeah, I have this great picture in my digital clutter that I'll put in stories of me just covered in the blue beat runoff drink.
所以，没错，我那堆数字杂物里有张很棒的照片，我会把它发到快拍里，照片里我浑身都是那种蓝色饮料的残留物。

677
00:30:40.110 --> 00:30:41.330
How many takes did you do?
你们拍了多少条？

678
00:30:41.510 --> 00:30:41.950
Do you remember?
你还记得吗？

679
00:30:41.950 --> 00:30:43.270
I don't remember.
我不记得了。

680
00:30:43.430 --> 00:30:46.150
But I think we had to—I know we did two for sure.
但我认为我们必须——我知道我们肯定拍了两条。

681
00:30:46.390 --> 00:30:48.070
And I think we might have gotten it in two.
我觉得我们可能拍了两条就过了。

682
00:30:48.370 --> 00:30:48.750
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

683
00:30:49.070 --> 00:30:51.290
But it was a lot to clean up.
但清理起来很麻烦。

684
00:30:51.290 --> 00:30:59.450
Well, before we move on, I would like to give a guest star shout-out to The Doctor, who was played by Oliver Vakour.
好了，在继续之前，我想特别感谢一下客串明星“医生”，由奥利弗·瓦库尔饰演。

685
00:30:59.870 --> 00:31:01.970
He's done a mix of comedy and drama.
他演过不少喜剧和正剧。

686
00:31:01.970 --> 00:31:03.970
He was most recently in the Barbie movie.
他最近出演了《芭比》电影。

687
00:31:04.470 --> 00:31:12.170
And he co-created and wrote a fictional true crime podcast called The Angel of Vine, which stars Alfred Molina and Constance Zimmer.
他还共同创作并编写了一部虚构的真实犯罪播客《葡萄藤天使》，由阿尔弗雷德·莫里纳和康斯坦斯·齐默主演。

688
00:31:12.410 --> 00:31:12.910
Oh.
哦。

689
00:31:13.090 --> 00:31:13.930
Your friend Constance.
你的朋友康斯坦斯。

690
00:31:13.930 --> 00:31:14.610
I love Constance.
我喜欢康斯坦斯。

691
00:31:14.810 --> 00:31:14.870
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

692
00:31:15.870 --> 00:31:20.970
And Monk Crossover, my character kills Alfred Molina in Monk.
还有《神探阿蒙》的联动，我的角色在《神探阿蒙》里杀了阿尔弗雷德·莫里纳。

693
00:31:21.270 --> 00:31:22.090
There you go.
原来如此。

694
00:31:22.210 --> 00:31:22.710
There you go.
原来如此。

695
00:31:23.110 --> 00:31:26.330
Well, we're going to continue finding out what people did over the summer.
好了，我们继续看看大家暑假都做了些什么。

696
00:31:26.610 --> 00:31:29.310
Kevin shares that his summer was an emotional roller coaster.
凯文分享说他的夏天就像坐过山车一样，情绪起伏很大。

697
00:31:29.570 --> 00:31:35.090
I guess he was pulling into the parking lot, and he ran over a turtle, and then he tried to save him by gluing his shell back together.
我猜他当时正开车进停车场，结果压到了一只乌龟，然后他试图用胶水把它的壳粘回去来救它。

698
00:31:35.230 --> 00:31:36.410
But he's really not good at puzzles.
但他真的不擅长拼图。

699
00:31:36.410 --> 00:31:40.250
So he just kind of found random things on his desk to help make the shell.
所以他就在桌上随便找了些东西来帮忙拼凑那个壳。

700
00:31:40.410 --> 00:31:46.810
And then as he was trying to rebuild the shell, he just crushed it again with his knee, and then he had to rebuild it even better.
然后当他试图重建那个壳时，又不小心用膝盖把它压碎了，最后他不得不把它修得更好。

701
00:31:47.310 --> 00:31:50.370
But then he thinks maybe the turtle was dead the whole time.
但后来他又想，也许那只乌龟从头到尾都是死的。

702
00:31:50.550 --> 00:31:52.910
We got a fan question from Jenna F.
我们收到了一位来自加利福尼亚州洛杉矶的粉丝Jenna F.的提问，

703
00:31:53.090 --> 00:31:59.890
in Los Angeles, California, who would like to know if the documentary crew was on a break over the summer,
她想知道如果纪录片摄制组在夏天休息的话，

704
00:31:59.890 --> 00:32:04.690
how did they get all the footage of Kevin running over the turtle and gluing it back together?
他们是怎么拍到凯文开车碾过乌龟又把它粘回去的所有镜头的？

705
00:32:04.690 --> 00:32:05.330
Jenna F.
Jenna F.

706
00:32:05.470 --> 00:32:07.990
has caught a lot of continuity errors in this episode.
在这集里发现了很多连贯性错误。

707
00:32:08.190 --> 00:32:09.650
Well, she has questions.
嗯，她确实有问题要问。

708
00:32:10.010 --> 00:32:12.610
I found some fun stuff online about this episode.
我在网上发现了一些关于这一集的有趣内容。

709
00:32:12.830 --> 00:32:17.610
First of all, there was a great fan catch about the moment where Kevin runs over the turtle.
首先，有一位粉丝很敏锐地捕捉到了凯文碾过乌龟的那个瞬间。

710
00:32:17.770 --> 00:32:21.050
They did a side-by-side of when Michael Scott hits Meredith.
他们把这一幕和迈克尔·斯科特撞到梅雷迪斯的场景做了对比。

711
00:32:21.410 --> 00:32:29.950
The moments are framed exactly the same, and both characters go from this moment of, like, being really happy to these looks of, like, oh, s***.
这两个镜头的构图完全一样，而且两个角色都是从那种非常开心的状态，瞬间变成了“噢，糟了”的表情。

712
00:32:30.610 --> 00:32:31.210
That's funny.
那太搞笑了。

713
00:32:31.210 --> 00:32:32.550
And they did a side-by-side.
他们还做了个对比视频。

714
00:32:32.550 --> 00:32:33.870
I'm going to share it in stories.
我打算把它分享到快拍里。

715
00:32:34.690 --> 00:32:37.810
There was also some online chatter about Kevin's turtle.
网上还有关于凯文那只乌龟的讨论。

716
00:32:38.190 --> 00:32:40.450
Here's something I found on a Reddit thread.
这是我在Reddit的一个帖子里发现的内容。

717
00:32:41.090 --> 00:32:44.910
A user said, Season 9, Episode 1, New Guys.
有用户说，第九季第一集《新来的家伙》。

718
00:32:45.210 --> 00:32:48.590
Is Kevin's turtle an allegory for the show?
凯文的乌龟是不是这部剧的隐喻？

719
00:32:48.810 --> 00:32:52.690
Was Greg Daniels acknowledging the state of the show through Kevin?
格雷格·丹尼尔斯是不是通过凯文在暗示这部剧的现状？

720
00:32:53.110 --> 00:32:54.890
Is the turtle the show?
乌龟就是这部剧吗？

721
00:32:55.090 --> 00:32:56.390
Is Greg Kevin?
格雷格就是凯文吗？

722
00:32:57.230 --> 00:32:58.490
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

723
00:33:03.640 --> 00:33:10.560
Was the show, like, run over and then he was trying to piece it back together only to discover that it was dead?
难道这部剧就像是被车碾过，而他试图把它拼凑回去，结果发现它早就死了？

724
00:33:10.700 --> 00:33:11.320
Oh, no.
噢，不。

725
00:33:11.860 --> 00:33:13.260
I mean, I hope not.
我是说，我希望不是这样。

726
00:33:13.420 --> 00:33:13.920
I know.
我知道。

727
00:33:13.920 --> 00:33:16.960
So, now we're going to hear about Jim and Pam's summer.
那么，现在我们要来聊聊吉姆和帕姆的夏天了。

728
00:33:17.240 --> 00:33:18.720
They have a talking head together.
他们一起接受了采访。

729
00:33:18.920 --> 00:33:21.200
And Pam sort of says nothing new happened.
帕姆说好像没什么新鲜事发生。

730
00:33:21.200 --> 00:33:23.620
But then Jim says, what are you talking about?
但吉姆却说，你在说什么呢？

731
00:33:23.760 --> 00:33:26.500
You did that mural in the kids' room.
你不是在孩子房间画了壁画吗？

732
00:33:26.960 --> 00:33:27.220
Yeah.
没错。

733
00:33:27.620 --> 00:33:30.880
Lady, I want you to know that was my pitch as producer.
女士，我想让你知道，那是作为制片人的我提出来的点子。

734
00:33:31.480 --> 00:33:32.000
Hey!
嘿！

735
00:33:32.780 --> 00:33:39.960
For Season 9, one of the things we talked about was Pam's art and how could this come back into her life?
对于第九季，我们讨论的事情之一就是帕姆的艺术，以及这如何能重新回到她的生活中？

736
00:33:40.220 --> 00:33:42.720
And how could she be expressed creatively?
她又该如何进行创意表达？

737
00:33:43.320 --> 00:33:45.780
And my son had a mural in his nursery.
我儿子的婴儿房里就有一幅壁画。

738
00:33:46.000 --> 00:33:46.980
So did my daughter.
我女儿的房间里也有。

739
00:33:47.180 --> 00:33:50.360
We both loved this little detail of our nurseries.
我们都很喜欢婴儿房里的这个小细节。

740
00:33:50.680 --> 00:33:55.420
And so I said, what if Pam starts painting murals?
所以我说，如果帕姆开始画壁画会怎样？

741
00:33:55.620 --> 00:33:58.360
If this becomes kind of a side gig for her?
如果这成了她的副业呢？

742
00:33:58.480 --> 00:34:00.880
Because we know she's not going to do graphic design.
因为我们知道她不会去搞平面设计。

743
00:34:00.880 --> 00:34:02.160
She didn't like it.
她不喜欢那个。

744
00:34:02.260 --> 00:34:03.300
She didn't take to it.
她不适合那一行。

745
00:34:03.460 --> 00:34:07.640
I said, she is a paint-on-canvas kind of person.
我说，她就是那种适合在画布上作画的人。

746
00:34:08.380 --> 00:34:09.960
Let's follow that thread.
我们顺着这条线索发展下去吧。

747
00:34:10.260 --> 00:34:13.520
So we're starting with this mural in Philip's room.
所以我们从菲利普房间里的这幅壁画开始。

748
00:34:13.880 --> 00:34:14.860
I love that.
我喜欢这个点子。

749
00:34:15.760 --> 00:34:19.180
And now Pam is going to gush on Jim a little bit.
现在帕姆要对吉姆大加赞赏一番了。

750
00:34:19.360 --> 00:34:20.360
She says, you know what?
她说，你知道吗？

751
00:34:20.720 --> 00:34:23.340
Jim's friend is starting a sports marketing company.
吉姆的朋友正在创办一家体育营销公司。

752
00:34:23.340 --> 00:34:26.320
And it was based on an idea that Jim had back in college.
而且这还是基于吉姆大学时的一个想法。

753
00:34:26.720 --> 00:34:27.180
Yeah.
是啊。

754
00:34:27.320 --> 00:34:29.580
And he says he wanted Jim to be part of the company.
他说他想让吉姆加入这家公司。

755
00:34:29.580 --> 00:34:31.780
But, you know, it's happening in Philly.
但你知道，公司在费城。

756
00:34:31.780 --> 00:34:33.660
And that didn't really work for their family.
这对他们的家庭来说不太合适。

757
00:34:33.840 --> 00:34:35.360
But still, how cool, right?
不过还是很酷，对吧？

758
00:34:35.960 --> 00:34:36.260
Yeah.
是啊。

