我在想，邀请礼仪到底是什么样的？

1108
00:50:42.570 --> 00:50:44.370
I went to emilypoSt.com.
我去了 emilypoSt.com 网站。

1109
00:50:45.070 --> 00:50:47.570
Here's what they say for a few different types of gatherings.
这是他们针对几种不同聚会给出的建议。

1110
00:50:48.390 --> 00:50:51.050
Anniversary party, three to six weeks.
周年纪念派对，提前三到六周。

1111
00:50:51.510 --> 00:50:52.190
Notice.
注意。

1112
00:50:52.570 --> 00:50:53.150
Notice.
注意。

1113
00:50:53.530 --> 00:50:53.830
Okay.
好的。

1114
00:50:54.470 --> 00:50:56.950
Holiday dinner, two weeks to two months.
节日晚餐，提前两周到两个月。

1115
00:50:57.550 --> 00:50:58.310
Okay.
好的。

1116
00:50:59.390 --> 00:51:02.030
Formal dinner, three to six weeks.
正式晚宴，提前三到六周。

1117
00:51:03.570 --> 00:51:05.810
Graduation party, three weeks.
毕业派对，提前三周。

1118
00:51:05.970 --> 00:51:06.170
Notice.
注意。

1119
00:51:07.150 --> 00:51:09.730
Lunch or tea, a few days to two weeks.
午餐或下午茶，提前几天到两周。

1120
00:51:10.050 --> 00:51:15.070
They did not have any tips for how long in advance you invite someone to a concert.
他们没有关于提前多久邀请别人参加演唱会的建议。

1121
00:51:15.450 --> 00:51:20.230
But I did find a Reddit thread inspired by this episode that said around three months.
但我确实找到了一个受这集启发的 Reddit 帖子，上面说大约三个月。

1122
00:51:20.510 --> 00:51:21.310
Well, listen.
嗯，听着。

1123
00:51:21.310 --> 00:51:26.030
If you want to go see a Taylor Swift concert, you might need to talk about it 10 months in advance.
如果你想去看泰勒·斯威夫特的演唱会，你可能得提前十个月就开始商量了。

1124
00:51:26.030 --> 00:51:27.170
A year in advance.
提前一年。

1125
00:51:27.390 --> 00:51:27.710
Yes.
没错。

1126
00:51:27.970 --> 00:51:30.330
So sometimes I think it depends on who's playing.
所以我认为有时这取决于谁在演出。

1127
00:51:31.090 --> 00:51:33.930
Well, Clark is going to tell Dwight he'll be busy in 10 months.
好吧，克拉克要告诉德怀特他十个月后没空。

1128
00:51:34.170 --> 00:51:34.510
Yeah.
是啊。

1129
00:51:34.590 --> 00:51:35.990
He's pretty sure he's busy that night.
他很确定那天晚上他有事。

1130
00:51:36.090 --> 00:51:36.250
Yeah.
是啊。

1131
00:51:36.730 --> 00:51:37.950
So Dwight's going to pivot.
所以德怀特要转换话题了。

1132
00:51:38.290 --> 00:51:39.970
He's like, dude, what's up with you?
他就像是说，伙计，你怎么回事？

1133
00:51:40.050 --> 00:51:41.230
Like, let's talk farming.
咱们聊聊务农吧。

1134
00:51:41.550 --> 00:51:41.730
Yeah.
是啊。

1135
00:51:41.810 --> 00:51:43.990
Are you a fruit guy or a root guy?
你是喜欢种水果还是种根茎类作物？

1136
00:51:46.210 --> 00:51:50.290
And Clark said, is this some sort of code for gay stuff?
然后克拉克说，这是某种关于同性恋的暗语吗？

1137
00:51:50.290 --> 00:51:53.810
Because, I mean, I'm totally fine with it, but I'm into the ladies.
因为，我是说，我完全没意见，但我喜欢的是女性。

1138
00:51:54.770 --> 00:51:56.730
Ah, spoken like a true root man.
啊，说得真像个地道的根茎类作物男。

1139
00:51:57.030 --> 00:52:02.450
And then Clark says, hey, if you're ever swamped, maybe I could take some of your sales calls.
然后克拉克说，嘿，如果你哪天忙不过来，也许我可以帮你接一些销售电话。

1140
00:52:03.070 --> 00:52:03.890
Oh, no.
噢，不。

1141
00:52:04.230 --> 00:52:05.410
Now Dwight is done.
现在德怀特彻底死心了。

1142
00:52:05.670 --> 00:52:06.870
You're not my son anymore.
你不再是我的儿子了。

1143
00:52:07.170 --> 00:52:08.170
I'm over you.
我受够你了。

1144
00:52:08.750 --> 00:52:09.710
It's done.
结束了。

1145
00:52:10.010 --> 00:52:10.910
It's a quick turn.
这转折真快。

1146
00:52:11.130 --> 00:52:11.470
Oh, yeah.
噢，是啊。

1147
00:52:11.470 --> 00:52:15.650
Dwight is going to go warn Jim, I think the new guys are trying to take our jobs.
德怀特要去警告吉姆，我想那几个新人想抢我们的饭碗。

1148
00:52:15.830 --> 00:52:16.010
Yeah.
是啊。

1149
00:52:16.650 --> 00:52:22.830
And so Jim immediately decides to mess with him and says, oh, yeah, that must be what Pete
于是吉姆立刻决定捉弄他，说，噢，是啊，那一定是皮特

